# Include / require scope

`require` shares the caller’s variable scope. Partials see `$viewer`, `$csrfToken`, `$article`, and anything else the page left in scope. That is powerful and brittle.

Do:

- Before `header.php`, set the usual chrome vars: `$title`, `$viewer`, `$csrfToken`, and flash/alert when needed.
- Keep partials dumb: they render fields, they do not load data.
- Name page-local vars clearly so accidental leakage into partials is obvious.

Do not:

- Rely on a partial defining a variable the next page “happens” to need.
- Build a View/renderer class to paper over scope until the pain is concrete.

❌ Partial that calls repositories  
✅ Page loads data, then `require` header / preview / footer
